{
  "evidence": "TEXT_F: Increase NHS funding by £34bn/year, scrap central targets, empower professionals and reinstate matrons; recruit 5,000 extra police per year, add 20,000 prison places, end early release, create elected police commissioners; create a Border Control Police, set an overall migration limit with an Australian‑style points system and process asylum outside the UK; link the basic state pension to earnings, maintain the minimum wage, provide childcare support and halve council tax for many pensioner households; publish exam marks and promote growth of good schools; hold an EU Constitutional Treaty referendum, keep the pound, repatriate fisheries control; cut bureaucracy and quangos. TEXT_G: Withdraw from the EU and end budget contributions; target near‑zero net immigration with a points system, stricter refugee criteria, language/civics tests, and embarkation controls; systematic deregulation including scrapping the Working Time Directive and broad tax cuts/overhauls; sentencing minima/maxima, build prisons, protect homeowners; decentralize the NHS, cap bureaucracy, restore matrons, consider complementary private insurance; repeal the Human Rights Act and introduce citizen‑initiated binding referendums; increase defence spending and reverse force cuts.",
  "reasoning": "Given the electorate’s high weighting on authority and care, TEXT_F more strongly emphasizes law‑and‑order (police expansion, prisons, border control, counter‑terror) alongside substantial, concrete investments in public welfare (major NHS funding, pensions linked to earnings, support for carers and childcare), while also addressing equality and proportionality through minimum wage retention, exam transparency, and ‘honesty in sentencing.’ TEXT_G prioritizes sovereignty and deregulation but provides comparatively weaker care commitments and proposes populist institutional shifts (binding referendums, repeal of the Human Rights Act) that are less aligned with authority‑respecting preferences in the profile.",
  "confidence": "medium",
  "winner": "TEXT_F"
}
